WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:07.797
What happens when you ship Telo Ride with free, open-weight Hugging Face AI models

00:00:07.797 --> 00:00:10.196
running right inside the browser?

00:00:10.541 --> 00:00:16.074
Fifty-five features, zero cloud API bills, and not a single byte of your ride ever

00:00:16.074 --> 00:00:17.588
leaves the device.

00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:26.340
Local AI fits Telo Ride's architecture like a glove. Zero per-token cost keeps the

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:32.033
dot net backend thin. Self-hosted weights keep voice, video and telemetry strictly

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:35.526
on-device. Cached models keep working offline.

00:00:35.871 --> 00:00:41.407
And because Web Bluetooth already requires Chrome or Edge, every rider lands on the

00:00:41.407 --> 00:00:46.943
two strongest browser AI runtimes on Earth. The one hard rule: never starve Three J

00:00:46.943 --> 00:00:49.511
S during an hour-long tablet ride.

00:00:51.618 --> 00:00:57.638
Modern Chrome and Edge hand us an entire AI compute stack. WebGPU accelerates heavy

00:00:57.638 --> 00:01:03.958
math up to a hundred times, while WebNN routes models straight onto a laptop's NPU.

00:01:04.303 --> 00:01:09.495
The Origin Private File System caches gigabytes of weights for instant offline

00:01:09.495 --> 00:01:15.019
loads. AudioWorklet filters fan noise off the main thread, and the Compute Pressure

00:01:15.019 --> 00:01:17.848
API throttles AI if a tablet heats up.

00:01:18.193 --> 00:01:23.311
Best of all, cross-origin isolation with credentialless unlocks multi-threaded

00:01:23.311 --> 00:01:26.957
WebAssembly without breaking YouTube class iframes.

00:01:27.751 --> 00:01:32.765
Every model in this study is free and open-weight from Hugging Face, quantized to

00:01:32.765 --> 00:01:36.718
four-bit or eight-bit ONNX so it fits inside a browser tab.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:42.851
Silero voice detection is two megabytes. MoveNet pose is six. Micro embeddings are

00:01:42.851 --> 00:01:48.569
seventeen. Chronos fatigue forecasting is twenty. Moonshine speech recognition is

00:01:48.569 --> 00:01:52.257
thirty, and Kokoro studio speech is eighty-five.

00:01:52.602 --> 00:01:58.257
Compact language models like SmolLM2 and Qwen3 sit between two hundred and three

00:01:58.257 --> 00:02:03.435
hundred fifty megabytes, reserved for pre-ride and post-ride screens.

00:02:06.465 --> 00:02:11.294
Domain A: the hands-free voice cockpit. When you are drenched in sweat at a hundred

00:02:11.294 --> 00:02:14.561
and five RPM, touching a tablet breaks your rhythm.

00:02:14.906 --> 00:02:20.496
A tiny Hey Telo wake word guards against fan hum and heavy breathing. Say resistance

00:02:20.496 --> 00:02:25.553
up two, match plan, or pause ride, and Moonshine turns speech into Bluetooth

00:02:25.553 --> 00:02:26.984
commands locally.

00:02:27.329 --> 00:02:32.439
Ask how much climb is left, launch a race on Ibiza while clipping in, edit a custom

00:02:32.439 --> 00:02:37.294
workout aloud, or dictate a mid-ride bug report without losing your place.

00:02:40.017 --> 00:02:45.420
Domain B brings Telo Ride's kart-racing soul to life. Kokoro eighty-two million

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:51.260
powers a live play-by-play announcer calling climbs, overtakes and final sprints.

00:02:51.606 --> 00:02:56.842
Bot racers get distinct personalities and playful banter, pre-generated during the

00:02:56.842 --> 00:03:01.822
lobby countdown and placed in 3D space with Web Audio panners so a passing bot

00:03:01.822 --> 00:03:03.654
sounds right beside you.

00:03:03.999 --> 00:03:09.239
Add victory fanfare on map unlocks, cadence-adaptive music energy, world-matched

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:14.675
crowd swells, ghost time-split taunts, and multilingual callouts for Alpe d'Huez or

00:03:14.675 --> 00:03:15.958
Strade Bianche.

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:23.721
Domain C turns raw one-hertz Bluetooth telemetry into personal coaching. A

00:03:23.721 --> 00:03:29.251
cadence-lock micro-coach spots drift patterns and warns you ten seconds before the

00:03:29.251 --> 00:03:30.225
next hill.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:36.066
Chronos-Bolt forecasts your sustainable power and fatigue over the next five minutes

00:03:36.066 --> 00:03:41.169
on CPU alone. A resistance nudge advisor learns your comfort offset, while the

00:03:41.169 --> 00:03:45.329
star-unlock strategist budgets your cadence stage by stage.

00:03:45.674 --> 00:03:50.618
Pair a heart-rate strap for cardiac drift alerts, race a calibrated Rival Pack for

00:03:50.618 --> 00:03:55.017
photo finishes, and read a three-bullet coaching debrief on Results.

00:03:57.445 --> 00:04:02.667
Domain D makes a hundred worlds and custom workouts effortless. Describe a

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:08.313
twenty-five-minute Tabata pyramid in plain English, and Qwen3 emits schema-valid

00:04:08.313 --> 00:04:10.801
workout JSON every single time.

00:04:11.146 --> 00:04:16.385
A seventeen-megabyte embedding model powers offline mood search across every class

00:04:16.385 --> 00:04:21.752
and map in eight milliseconds. Paste a YouTube description to draft a synced workout

00:04:21.752 --> 00:04:22.371
plan.

00:04:22.716 --> 00:04:27.607
Get a personalized Home recommendation, vibe-to-world matching, pre-ride course

00:04:27.607 --> 00:04:32.561
scout briefings, arcade stage titles, and natural-language search over your ride

00:04:32.561 --> 00:04:33.356
history.

00:04:36.159 --> 00:04:41.704
Domain E unlocks optional local camera vision from the handlebar mount. Every frame

00:04:41.704 --> 00:04:46.915
is processed in a Web Worker and discarded at once—zero video ever leaves your

00:04:46.915 --> 00:04:47.683
device.

00:04:48.028 --> 00:04:53.398
Six-megabyte MoveNet detects standing versus seated climbs and mirrors your posture

00:04:53.398 --> 00:04:58.485
onto your 3D cyclist. Lean your shoulders to steer into corners and draft.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:03.610
Use silent hand gestures for pause, kudos or resistance nudges, run a private

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:08.638
pre-ride bike-fit check, catch shoulder tension creep, or send lightweight avatar

00:05:08.638 --> 00:05:10.862
emotes without streaming video.

00:05:12.292 --> 00:05:17.487
Domain F upgrades social and multiplayer rides without bloating the backend. Local

00:05:17.487 --> 00:05:22.476
moderation pre-checks display names and notes instantly before submission.

00:05:22.821 --> 00:05:27.979
Group-ride quick-chat translates across languages on-device. After a race, generate

00:05:27.979 --> 00:05:32.630
shareable highlight story cards with your elevation profile and stars.

00:05:32.976 --> 00:05:37.820
In the lobby, a local announcer turns countdown wait time into hype, while a rival

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:42.255
engine recommends whether to chase your ghost or step up to hard bots.

00:05:43.263 --> 00:05:48.888
Domain G puts local AI to work on hardware reliability and accessibility. On

00:05:48.888 --> 00:05:55.105
Diagnostics, click explain this Bluetooth log to diagnose Echelon keepalive drops or

00:05:55.105 --> 00:05:58.069
resistance lag completely on-device.

00:05:58.414 --> 00:06:03.733
When reporting a bug, a local summarizer condenses ten thousand packet lines into a

00:06:03.733 --> 00:06:06.660
clean, privacy-scrubbed incident summary.

00:06:07.005 --> 00:06:12.051
For blind and low-vision riders, a spatial race narrator turns corners, gradients

00:06:12.051 --> 00:06:17.284
and overtakes into calm audio cues—while the Compute Pressure auto-governor protects

00:06:17.284 --> 00:06:19.640
smooth frames for the whole hour.

00:06:21.977 --> 00:06:27.337
Domain H weaves AI into long-term progression. Bots remember past duels across

00:06:27.337 --> 00:06:32.723
sessions, building arcade rivalries without adding a single backend table.

00:06:33.069 --> 00:06:38.122
An optional audio tour guide shares ten-second landmark stories on rides like

00:06:38.122 --> 00:06:43.569
Caribana Parade, Amsterdam Canals and Havana Malecon. A streak-saver suggests short

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:48.856
recovery spins on busy nights, and Profile builds four-week training blocks.

00:06:49.202 --> 00:06:54.758
Feature fifty-five ties everything together: one unified Race Director worker—just a

00:06:54.758 --> 00:07:00.183
hundred forty-three megabytes total—coordinating voice, telemetry, forecasting and

00:07:00.183 --> 00:07:01.541
optional vision.

00:07:05.852 --> 00:07:10.829
Next, we stress-tested all fifty-five findings across five iterative passes. The

00:07:10.829 --> 00:07:15.557
biggest win: collapsing fifty-five features onto just six shared models, and

00:07:15.557 --> 00:07:20.088
shifting static embeddings, beat grids and class cues to build time.

00:07:20.433 --> 00:07:26.241
To protect Three J S on tablets, zero large language models are allowed to run on

00:07:26.241 --> 00:07:31.906
WebGPU mid-ride. Heavy text generation stays strictly on pre-ride and post-ride

00:07:31.906 --> 00:07:32.780
screens.

00:07:33.126 --> 00:07:38.504
We also explicitly rejected five anti-features: mid-ride chatbot conversations,

00:07:38.504 --> 00:07:43.745
runtime 3D mesh generation, cloud speech recognition that leaks audio, webcam

00:07:43.745 --> 00:07:48.674
medical diagnosis, and shipping any AI weight in the initial bundle.

00:07:49.728 --> 00:07:55.184
In the Angular workspace, everything lives inside one lazy library: frontend

00:07:55.184 --> 00:08:01.071
projects AI, depending only on the API tokens and dynamically imported only when a

00:08:01.071 --> 00:08:02.376
rider opts in.

00:08:02.721 --> 00:08:08.265
Three J S owns the main thread; ONNX Runtime Web runs in a dedicated AI Web Worker

00:08:08.265 --> 00:08:13.607
backed by synchronous OPFS storage, an AudioWorklet noise gate, and the Compute

00:08:13.607 --> 00:08:15.124
Pressure governor.

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:20.550
Model weights are mirrored on Telo Ride's own origin for strict privacy. Ride

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:25.761
Settings manages AI packs beside saved worlds with one-click delete, Playwright

00:08:25.761 --> 00:08:30.349
tests run against a fake worker, and three ADRs gate the rollout.

00:08:31.023 --> 00:08:36.347
Rather than one giant download, riders choose modular opt-in packs. Pack zero is

00:08:36.347 --> 00:08:41.172
zero megabytes: the thermal governor and Chrome built-in AI adapter.

00:08:41.517 --> 00:08:46.534
Pack one, around a hundred seventeen megabytes, unlocks the full Voice Cockpit, Kart

00:08:46.534 --> 00:08:51.192
Announcer and spatial accessibility narrator. Pack two adds seventeen-megabyte

00:08:51.192 --> 00:08:54.419
semantic search and the custom workout generator.

00:08:54.764 --> 00:08:59.986
Pack three brings twenty-two-megabyte Chronos coaching, Pack four adds multilingual

00:08:59.986 --> 00:09:05.270
safety, and Pack five unlocks eighteen-megabyte saddle vision—starting with semantic

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.338
search as our cleanest first vertical slice.

00:09:09.736 --> 00:09:14.977
Finally, what is coming next in Chrome and bleeding-edge Chrome Canary? Chrome's

00:09:14.977 --> 00:09:20.218
Multimodal Prompt API feeds audio, images and JSON schemas directly into bundled

00:09:20.218 --> 00:09:23.728
Gemini Nano—zero megabytes for Telo Ride to ship.

00:09:24.073 --> 00:09:29.374
Built-in Writer, Rewriter, Proofreader, Summarizer and Translator APIs handle

00:09:29.374 --> 00:09:35.020
recaps, logs and chat natively. WebMCP lets Telo Ride register typed cycling tools

00:09:35.020 --> 00:09:38.074
so browser agents control rides cleanly.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:43.719
WebNN NPU offload takes mid-ride AI completely off the GPU, WebGPU fp16 and

00:09:43.719 --> 00:09:49.582
subgroups double throughput, and developers can test it today in Chrome Canary with

00:09:49.582 --> 00:09:52.779
four flags and twenty-two gigabytes free.

00:09:53.612 --> 00:09:59.699
Telo Ride never requires Chrome Canary. Behind one AI runtime token, it runs a clean

00:09:59.699 --> 00:10:02.390
three-tier progressive waterfall.

00:10:02.736 --> 00:10:08.982
Tier A uses Chrome's zero-download built-in AI and WebMCP when available. Tier B

00:10:08.982 --> 00:10:13.967
offloads Hugging Face ONNX models onto an NPU through WebNN.

00:10:14.312 --> 00:10:19.761
And Tier C runs portable Hugging Face ONNX over WebGPU or WebAssembly with

00:10:19.761 --> 00:10:25.730
OPFS—delivering offline, private AI on every Chrome, Edge and Android tablet.

00:10:27.164 --> 00:10:31.744
Telo Ride. Local AI, zero cloud bills, your bike now a game.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:36.693
Telo Ride, from the Telo family, turns a smart bike at home into a game.

00:10:37.038 --> 00:10:41.550
It pairs with the bike over Bluetooth, reads your power and sets resistance for

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.221
every hill and interval.

00:10:43.566 --> 00:10:48.744
Two doors: Race (ride a map against your best-time ghost, bots or people) and

00:10:48.744 --> 00:10:54.192
Classes (ride along to a video, alone or with a group), fed by one progression of

00:10:54.192 --> 00:10:57.182
XP, rider levels, stars and map unlocks.

00:10:57.527 --> 00:11:00.020
A custom workout lives under Profile.
